1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,920
From inspected laundry to automated storage and customer pickup. This is the
v7 project concept.

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:11,920
Staff register the garment and load the shared port. After the door is
locked and reset, the robot grips its rigid adapter.

3
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:15,920
The adapter seats on an empty carrier. Item identity and storage position
are confirmed.

4
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:22,920
Staff place shoes in a tray on the folding shelf. Closing, locking and
resetting the port permits automatic handling.

5
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:27,920
The telescopic fork deposits the tray on shelf S02. The inventory record is
confirmed.

6
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:32,920
The customer authenticates with a pickup number or QR code. The requested
items are checked and reserved.

7
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:37,920
The garment chain indexes the requested carrier. Position locking and item
identification precede pickup.

8
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:42,920
The robot grips the rigid adapter, not the fabric, and lifts it clear of the
support pin.

9
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,920
The receiving saddle takes the load. Seating and latch confirmation precede
gripper release.

10
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:53,920
The receiver travels 730 mm horizontally and lowers 300 mm. The inner door
is locked before customer access.

11
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:58,920
The customer takes the hanger and garment. The transport adapter remains
inside.

12
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:04,920
After customer-door locking, the receiver returns and the robot places the
empty adapter back on H05.

13
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:11,920
The three-stage fork extends 600 mm and raises the tray 20 mm. The lift
brings it to the belt transfer height.

14
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:16,920
Linked rollers move the tray to the identification stop. The robot grips its
handle.

15
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:22,920
The robot raises the tray above the pedestal, transfers it, lowers it onto
the output rollers and retreats.

16
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:27,920
The tray enters the shoe compartment while the outer shutter is locked. The
inner shutter then closes.

17
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:32,920
The customer takes only the shoes. The reusable tray remains in the
compartment.

18
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:40,920
After the outer shutter closes, the empty tray returns inside. The robot
places it back on the infeed.

19
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:46,920
The belt, lift and fork return the empty tray to S02. Pickup and carrier-
return records complete the order.

20
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:53,920
Door locking, position, identity and grip confirmation gate the next action.
Faults hold motion for operator review and reset.

21
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:59,920
Staff loading, automated delivery, customer pickup and carrier return form
one connected workflow. Illustrated with the v7 model.
